MENTOR: So Pop grows from the middle of its bottom edge. Right now Pop's pivot is at its center.

**Anchor Point is where the pivot sits inside the layer; Position is where that pivot sits in the comp.** If you change Anchor Point by itself, the layer slides so the new pivot lands where the old one was. Pan Behind changes both together, so nothing moves on screen.

At 4.3 s, Pop is the small square down in the lower-left corner of the frame. Once the pivot is on its bottom edge, Pop will grow up from that edge and stay sitting on it, instead of growing out in every direction.

Pop is full size at 4.3 s. Put the playhead there first, then set its pivot.

To set it:
1. Press **Y** for the Pan Behind tool.
2. Select Pop in the timeline so its crosshair shows.
3. Press **A**, then **Shift+P**, so you can watch Anchor Point and Position both change.
4. Start your drag right on Pop's crosshair and drag it to the middle of Pop's bottom edge.

Give it a try, and say "done" when you've set it.

I could show you on Door first, if you like.

